            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-59530",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/quic-go/quic-go: quic-go Crash Due to Premature HANDSHAKE_DONE Frame"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "quic-go is an implementation of the QUIC protocol in Go. In versions prior to 0.49.0, 0.54.1, and 0.55.0, a misbehaving or malicious server can cause a denial-of-service (DoS) attack on the quic-go client by triggering an assertion failure, leading to a process crash. This requires no authentication and can be exploited during the handshake phase. This was observed in the wild with certain server implementations. quic-go needs to be able to handle misbehaving server implementations, including those that prematurely send a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame. Versions 0.49.0, 0.54.1, and 0.55.0 discard Initial keys when receiving a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame, thereby correctly handling premature HANDSHAKE_DONE frames."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-59530",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-59530\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: github.com/quic-go/quic-go\nFixed Version: 0.49.1, 0.54.1\nLink: [CVE-2025-59530](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-59530)\nquic-go is an implementation of the QUIC protocol in Go. In versions prior to 0.49.0, 0.54.1, and 0.55.0, a misbehaving or malicious server can cause a denial-of-service (DoS) attack on the quic-go client by triggering an assertion failure, leading to a process crash. This requires no authentication and can be exploited during the handshake phase. This was observed in the wild with certain server implementations. quic-go needs to be able to handle misbehaving server implementations, including those that prematurely send a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame. Versions 0.49.0, 0.54.1, and 0.55.0 discard Initial keys when receiving a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame, thereby correctly handling premature HANDSHAKE_DONE frames.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-59530**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|github.com/quic-go/quic-go|0.49.1, 0.54.1|[CVE-2025-59530](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-59530)|\n\nquic-go is an implementation of the QUIC protocol in Go. In versions prior to 0.49.0, 0.54.1, and 0.55.0, a misbehaving or malicious server can cause a denial-of-service (DoS) attack on the quic-go client by triggering an assertion failure, leading to a process crash. This requires no authentication and can be exploited during the handshake phase. This was observed in the wild with certain server implementations. quic-go needs to be able to handle misbehaving server implementations, including those that prematurely send a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame. Versions 0.49.0, 0.54.1, and 0.55.0 discard Initial keys when receiving a HANDSHAKE_DONE frame, thereby correctly handling premature HANDSHAKE_DONE frames."
              },
