            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-64702",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "github.com/quic-go/quic-go/http3: quic-go HTTP/3 QPACK Header Expansion DoS"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "quic-go is an implementation of the QUIC protocol in Go. Versions 0.56.0 and below are vulnerable to excessive memory allocation through quic-go's HTTP/3 client and server implementations by sending a QPACK-encoded HEADERS frame that decodes into a large header field section (many unique header names and/or large values). The implementation builds an http.Header (used on the http.Request and http.Response, respectively), while only enforcing limits on the size of the (QPACK-compressed) HEADERS frame, but not on the decoded header, leading to memory exhaustion. This issue is fixed in version 0.57.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-64702",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-64702\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/quic-go/quic-go\nFixed Version: 0.57.0\nLink: [CVE-2025-64702](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-64702)\nquic-go is an implementation of the QUIC protocol in Go. Versions 0.56.0 and below are vulnerable to excessive memory allocation through quic-go's HTTP/3 client and server implementations by sending a QPACK-encoded HEADERS frame that decodes into a large header field section (many unique header names and/or large values). The implementation builds an http.Header (used on the http.Request and http.Response, respectively), while only enforcing limits on the size of the (QPACK-compressed) HEADERS frame, but not on the decoded header, leading to memory exhaustion. This issue is fixed in version 0.57.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-64702**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/quic-go/quic-go|0.57.0|[CVE-2025-64702](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-64702)|\n\nquic-go is an implementation of the QUIC protocol in Go. Versions 0.56.0 and below are vulnerable to excessive memory allocation through quic-go's HTTP/3 client and server implementations by sending a QPACK-encoded HEADERS frame that decodes into a large header field section (many unique header names and/or large values). The implementation builds an http.Header (used on the http.Request and http.Response, respectively), while only enforcing limits on the size of the (QPACK-compressed) HEADERS frame, but not on the decoded header, leading to memory exhaustion. This issue is fixed in version 0.57.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.3,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L",
